codex
Verdict: MAJOR

Findings:
- [major] Retrieval contract is not fully satisfied for this issue class mix — `docs/plans/README.md` says issues matching multiple classes must use the union of required sources. Issue `#2460` is labeled `cat:documentation` and `cat:harness`, but the plan’s `Resource Intelligence Summary` omits the documentation-class durable/transient boundary source (`#2209`) and any harness-specific sources (`config/agents/`, `.claude/rules/`). That leaves approval readiness unsupported against the repo’s own planning workflow.
- [major] The plan relies on the curated stale-reference guard without actually bringing the new docs under that guard — `Resource Intelligence Summary` cites `tests/docs/test_banned_stale_references.py` as the pattern “for a new contract doc,” but [tests/docs/test_banned_stale_references.py](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/tests/docs/test_banned_stale_references.py) hardcodes `STRICT_FILES` and does not include the planned new files under `docs/standards/`. `Files to Change` also omits that test/helper. As written, the new contract/checklist can ship outside the existing curated-doc stale-reference coverage.
- [minor] The bulk-artifact-store wording is still looser than the canonical placement rule — [docs/standards/DATA_PLACEMENT.md](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/standards/DATA_PLACEMENT.md) defines the repo-vs-`/mnt/ace/data/` decision with explicit thresholds (`>= 10 MB` or `>= 1000 files`), but the plan’s `Deliverable` and `Pseudocode` reduce that to “large, generated, or fast-growing artifacts.” That keeps `/mnt/ace/data` as an example, but it does not yet guarantee consistency with the existing standard.

Checks performed:
- Verified `docs/BUSINESS_BRAIN.md` names exactly four current tier-1 repos: `workspace-hub`, `digitalmodel`, `assetutilities`, `aceengineer-website`.
- Verified the plan explicitly repeats the scorecard negative-authority guard in `Pseudocode`, `TDD Test List`, and `Acceptance Criteria`.
- Verified the plan makes TDD sequencing explicit: write `tests/docs/test_tier1_indexing_contract.py` first, confirm failure, then edit docs.
- Verified `#2461`-`#2465` exist and align with the checklist/remediation split the plan claims.
- Verified the existing stale-reference guard only scans the hardcoded files in `STRICT_FILES`, and the helper only enforces the current banned-path patterns.
